clude: book title text, author name, metallic effects, gold, warm tones, line-art figures, icons, habit loops, meditating people, stairs, arrows. Keep it STARK: black + teal + white dominoes.\n```\n<truncated 2096 bytes>\n Clean cool white #FAFAFA. Very subtle grey grid pattern (like graph paper lines) at 5% opacity across the entire background. NOT warm cream — this is cool, modern white. No gradients, no vignette.\n\nLEFT THIRD (28% of frame): Real published \"Atomic Habits\" book by James Clear (Cornerstone Press, cream cover). Angled 12° clockwise, 3D perspective. Soft subtle shadow beneath — very light since the background is white. The book is NOT the hero here — it's the starting point.\n\nCENTER-RIGHT (the hero — 60% of frame): A vertical STACK of small blocks/bricks building upward in a curve. Starting from near the book's base:\n- Bottom blocks: tiny (3px height), pale pastel colors, closely packed\n- Each layer of blocks gets slightly larger and more saturated in color\n- The stack follows an exponential curve upward and to the right\n- Top blocks: large (40px height), vivid saturated colors\n- Block colors represent habit domains:\n  - Green #22C55E (health blocks)\n  - Blue #3B82F6 (learning blocks)\n  - Orange #F97316 (routine blocks)\n  - Purple #8B5CF6 (mindset blocks)\n- The blocks are clean geometric rectangles with tiny gaps between them\n- The overall shape of the stack traces an exponential growth curve\n\nALONG THE CURVE (text): \n- \"TINY\" — physically tiny font, charcoal #1A1A2E, positioned near the bottom-left of the stack where blocks are small. Font: modern geometric sans-serif (Montserrat Bold). Size: about 3% of frame height.\n- \"→\" — a simple arrow, same charcoal color, connecting TINY to MASSIVE along the curve\n- \"MASSIVE\" — physically LARGE font, same charcoal #1A1A2E, positioned near the top-right of the stack where blocks are big. Size: about 15% of frame height.\n- The text size literally demonstrates the message — it GROWS as you read left to right\n\nBOTTOM CENTER: \"AUDIOBOOK 🎧\" in charcoal, small, clean modern font.\n\nDo NOT include: dark backgrounds, metallic text, gold, meditating figures, habit loop circles, domino chains, line art, sepia tones, warm browns. This is COLD, GEOMETRIC, MODERN.\n```","thinking":"**Generating Copy-Pasteable Prompts**\n\nI've taken the existing thumbnail prompts and am working on generating them in a format that the user can directly copy and paste. I'm focusing on providing each prompt individually and then considering how to combine them if the user needs that functionality.\n\n\n**Extracting & Presenting Prompts**\n\nI'm now focusing on directly presenting the image generation prompts. I've switched to the Gemini 3.1 Pro (High) model to ensure the best performance. My process involves extracting \"IMAGE GENERATION PROMPT\" blocks from the artifact and presenting them clearly in the chat response. These will be in code blocks, for immediate copy-paste access. I'm verifying I have the necessary context from the previous turn and ready to present the prompts to the user.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Composition**\n\nI'm now breaking down a detailed visual description to identify key compositional elements. I'm focusing on the positioning and sizes of the book, dominoes, and text, to ensure these are correctly interpreted for the image generation. I'm noting color palettes and how the elements interact within the frame. My goal is to capture the essence of the composition so the generated image matches the description closely.\n\n\n**Refining Prompts' Details**\n\nI'm working to refine this \"Broken Chain\" prompt, ensuring it excludes unwanted details. I've focused on keeping a stark visual style with black, teal, and white dominoes, specifically removing text from the book title and other elements. The prompt aims for a dark, cinematic composition and photorealistic details. My focus is on the contrast and the dynamic energy of the breaking chain, making