{"step_index":67,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T02:36:03Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 1 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. I am going to use the vidIQ website to get a response because you can get those answers in ten seconds. \n\nHere is the question: \n\nFor this channel, I don't have a thumbnail designer, a scriptwriter, or anything. I just have high-end AI models like Opus 4.6, notebookLM, and lots of APIs that can help me out. \n\nI want to ask about the thumbnails inside the image I am going to give you. I am going to upload them to the vidIQ website as well. Can you check if it can create similar thumbnails exactly like these if I upload the channel's thumbnails? If so, how? Please give me one or two responses using these thumbnails from the channel.                         ------------ use sop required\n2. I want all the responses in one prompt, man, so he can give me all the responses in .md files. Ask everything that you can ask, it costs only 10 rupees, and ask for the responses in .md files only.\n3. this is the result i got : Let me pull the concrete prompt at the end of the document so I execute exactly what it asks.Let me pull the actual detailed creative brief from the document — the specific book, text overlay, colors, and background specified in the generation prompts.I've got the reference style and the document's full spec. Let me load the design protocol so the prompts are built properly.Here's the complete package the document asks for — the reference visual DNA plus exact recreation prompts for all 5 books.🎨 Reference Visual DNA (from SoulArc Studios)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nElementSpecLayoutBook cover left third (25–35% width), angle-floating; title text right two-thirdsRead flowLeft→right: cover → big title → accent lineFontHeavy bold sans-serif, all-\n<truncated 18370 bytes>\nCT: media_1789869380983]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789869380983.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T01:58:19Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: atomic-habits-exceptional-thumbnails]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/atomic-habits-exceptional-thumbnails.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T02:36:03Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: atomic-habits-original-concepts]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/atomic-habits-original-concepts.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T02:23:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: soularc-forensic-analysis-and-prompt]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/soularc-forensic-analysis-and-prompt.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T02:03:07Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: soularc-thumbnail-replication-guide]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/soularc-thumbnail-replication-guide.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T23:48:12Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: vidiq-correction-prompt]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/vidiq-correction-prompt.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T00:07:03Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: vidiq-mega-prompt]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/vidiq-mega-prompt.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T23:49:58Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: vidiq-response-audit]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/vidiq-response-audit.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-20T02:11:02Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c\\.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl\n\n**IMPORTANT: this summary is just for your reference. You may respond to my previous and future messages, but DO NOT ACKNOWLEDGE THIS CHECKPOINT MESSAGE. JUST READ IT BUT DO NOT MENTION IT, RESPOND TO IT, OR TAKE ACTION BECAUSE OF IT.**","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":68,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T02:37:46Z","content":"Three completely different concepts this time. Here's why these are actually clickable:\n\n---\n\n### 🥇 Concept 2: \"The Rewired Brain\" — SAFEST BET\nA photorealistic brain split down the middle — left half tangled/chaotic (dark red), right half clean/organized (teal glow). Book at the base. Text: just \"BEFORE\" and \"AFTER.\"\n\n**Why this is exceptional:** SoulArc's brain thumbnails have **3.1 MILLION combined views**. Brains are PROVEN in this niche. But nobody shows a brain MID-TRANSFORMATION. The before/after split is the most instinctive visual in the world — at 120px on a phone, you see \"brain, two colors, something changed.\"\n\n---\n\n### 🥈 Concept 3: \"The 3:55 AM Decision\" — HIGHEST CEILING\nA dark bedroom. A phone screen glowing at 3:55 AM showing an audiobook player. Headphones beside it. Text: \"CAN'T STOP LISTENING.\"\n\n**Why this is exceptional:** It BREAKS THE FOURTH WALL. The viewer is sitting in a dark room, on their phone, right now. This thumbnail shows THEM. Nobody in the entire Hindi audiobook niche does this. The curiosity hook: \"Someone stayed up until 4 AM for this book? It must be THAT good.\"\n\n---\n\n### 🥉 Concept 1: \"The Lit Mind\" — CULTURALLY POWERFUL\nA human head silhouette with golden light exploding inside where the brain should be. The book below, open, radiating the light into the head. Text: \"YOUR MIND AFTER THIS BOOK.\"\n\n**Why this is exceptional:** \"Kitaab se gyan ki roshni\" — the light of knowledge from a book is a DEEPLY Indian cultural image. Every viewer instantly understands this visual. Gold-on-dark is SoulArc's highest-performing palette.\n\n---\n\n**My recommendation:** Generate Concept 2 first. If CTR is below 6% after 48 hours, swap to Concept 3. All three prompts are paste-ready in the artifact."}
{"step_index":69,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T02:49:20Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nI got a new idea. I love the background color of the \"Atomic Habits\" image, the person whose brain is popping and lighting up, and the tiny-to-massive growth graphic. \n\nThese are the three things I like, and I want them in a proper ratio so it looks like a thumbnail. \n\nFor the layout:\n• Put the head in the middle\n• Place the book on the left side\n• Position the tiny-to-massive growth graphic in between\n• Use the background of that \"Atomic Habits\" image for the whole thing                 So, what do you understand? \n\nFirst, tell me some short lines, and then create a whole prompt that you can customize for the best results. I have just given you the basic idea of the concept, so you can mix it up: like deciding which elements should be used, what the opacity should be, and which things should be highlighted. You can do all of this using your own skills. \n\nWhat are your thoughts on that?\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-20T08:19:20+05:30.\n\nThe user has uploaded 3 image(s):\n- C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789872304104.png\n- C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789872326940.png\n- C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789872340889.png\nYou can embed these images in an artifact if you need the USER to review them.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
